": "Whether MAHA-aligned outside spending and the final debate stretch tighten the race beyond the current high-single-digit polling range.", "confidence": "high", "notes": ["Open seat: Kim Reynolds (R) is not on the ballot."]}, "overview": "Kim Reynolds' retirement leaves Iowa's governorship open in a state that has leaned about six points Republican recently. Despite that, Democratic nominee Rob Sand has led Republican Zach Lahn in every public poll this fall, with margins from four to twelve points and an average near eight; Independent Sondra Wilson is also on the ballot. Rating outlets across the spectrum call the race a Democratic flip, from tilt to likely.\n\nPrediction markets put Sand's win chances near ninety percent, and The Gazette's editorial board has endorsed him. The counterweights are Iowa's Republican fundamentals, the open-seat dynamic, and roughly two million dollars in spending by RFK Jr.-aligned groups backing Lahn. The newest surveys show modest tightening from September's wider leads, but the Democratic edge remains well clear of the margin a single debate or advertising push would typically erase.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.8753, "margin": 5.7}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.8859, "margin": 6.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.8669, "margin": 6.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.8657, "margin": 6.0}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.8472, "margin": 6.0}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.8297, "margin": 5.5}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.8734, "margin": 6.0}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.8592, "margin": 5.5}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.8769, "margin": 6.0}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.8877, "margin": 6.0}, {"date": "2026-10-02", "p_dem": 0.8875, "margin": 6.5}, {"date": "2026-10-03", "p_dem": 0.895, "margin": 6.5}, {"date": "2026-10-04", "p_dem": 0.8938, "margin": 6.5}, {"date": "2026-10-05", "p_dem": 0.8853, "margin": 6.5}, {"date": "2026-10-06", "p_dem": 0.8878, "margin": 7.0}, {"date"